---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/url';
import { site } from '../site.config';
const title = 'Privacy Policy';
const description = `How ${site.name} handles data: no accounts, no uploads, no tracking cookies, minimal aggregate analytics.`;
const updated = site.launched;
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <article class="container container--narrow section prose">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: 'Home', url: '/' }, { name: 'Privacy', url: '/privacy/' }]} />
    <h1>{title}</h1>
    <p class="muted small">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    <h2>Summary</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>{site.name} does not require an account and does not ask for personal information.</li>
      <li>Photos and images you add are processed entirely in your browser (decoded, converted, compressed, resized) and are never uploaded to our servers — see the <a href={withBase('/privacy-proof/')}>privacy proof page</a> to verify this yourself.</li>
      <li>EXIF metadata, including GPS location, camera model and timestamp, is read locally only to warn you before export, and is always stripped from the file Pixlite produces. If a photo contains GPS coordinates, the warning links to OpenStreetMap (a third-party, non-tracking map service) so you can see the approximate location before it is stripped — that page only opens if you click it, and no coordinates are sent anywhere automatically.</li>
      <li>Pixlite does not store any preferences or history in your browser's local storage — the only thing kept between visits is your last-used conversion settings, encoded in the page URL itself if you bookmark or share it.</li>
      <li>We do not use advertising or tracking cookies.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      Analytics, if enabled at all, is one of two cookieless services — never both: <a href="https://plausible.io/privacy-focused-web-analytics" rel="noopener">Plausible Analytics</a> (an open-source,
      EU-hosted, GDPR-compliant analytics platform that does not use cookies or cross-site tracking), or a self-hosted
      beacon we operate that records only the page path, the referring site's domain, and an approximate device-width
      class (small/medium/large). Either way we collect only aggregate, cookieless data — never a per-person identifier,
      and never anything about the files you process. This data cannot identify you and is used solely to understand
      which pages are useful. Requests that send a "Do Not Track" signal are not counted.
    </p>
    <h2>Advertising and affiliate links</h2>
    <p>
      Some pages may show advertising or affiliate links to fund the service. If a third-party advertising provider is
      used, it may set cookies subject to its own policy and, where required by law, only after you give consent. Affiliate
      links are marked and never change the price you pay.
    </p>
    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>The site is served as static files from a content delivery network. Standard server logs (IP address, user agent, requested URL) may be kept briefly by the hosting provider for security and abuse prevention.</p>
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Under the GDPR, UK GDPR, CCPA and similar laws you may have rights of access, rectification, erasure and objection.
      Because we do not hold personal data about you, there is usually nothing to access or delete; if you believe
      otherwise, contact <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>
    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>The service is not directed at children under 13 and we do not knowingly collect data from them.</p>
    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>We will update this page when practices change and revise the date above.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
